# Agent Learnings Registry
<!-- ACTIVE LEARNING: Agents log mistakes here when they take >1 attempt.
     Categories enable fast lookup. Agents check here BEFORE retrying.

     FORMAT: | ID | Category | Trigger | Root Cause | Solution | Agent | Date |
     ID: LRN-{NNN} (sequential, permanent, never reused)
     Categories: SELECTOR, TIMING, LOGIC, DATA, SCOPE, FORMAT, NAVIGATION, AUTH

     AUTOMATED: task-context-builder injects relevant learnings into injectedContext.
     OWNERSHIP: Any agent may APPEND. Only Audit may EDIT/DELETE. -->

## Learnings

| ID | Category | Trigger | Root Cause | Solution | Agent | Date |
|----|----------|---------|------------|----------|-------|------|
| LRN-001 | NAVIGATION | page.goto ERR_NAME_NOT_RESOLVED on fabricated URL | Agent constructed URL from assumptions instead of reading config | Read BASE_URL from config/environments/.env.* — NEVER fabricate URLs. Use browser_navigate to known base, then click through UI | Planner | 2026-02-19 |
| LRN-002 | TIMING | browser_snapshot returned stale DOM | Snapshot taken immediately after navigate without wait | Always browser_wait_for(time:3) between navigate and snapshot (PLN-045) | Planner | 2026-02-19 |
| LRN-003 | FORMAT | TC IDs rejected by lint | Used wrong submodule code in TC ID | Read existing TC files first to match established pattern — check KNOWN_SUB_CODES in lint-test-cases.ts | Planner | 2026-02-19 |

| LRN-004 | SCOPE | Audit agent terminated without updating mistake registry | Treated Mode 1 checklist step 7 as optional | Registry update is MANDATORY — do not end turn until agent-mistakes.md is updated (AUD-016) | Audit | 2026-02-19 |

<!-- Seed entries above are derived from real historical mistakes. New entries appended below. -->

| LRN-005 | AUTH | White page after login — all tests show blank browser | OAuth token endpoint returned 400 — no diagnostic data captured to detect | Add runtime diagnostics: `page.on('response')` + auth chain capture + failure classification in AgentReporter. Agents must check `networkFailures[]` before blaming selectors | Copilot | 2026-02-24 |
| LRN-006 | SCOPE | Agents had diagnostic data (screenshotPath, tracePath, urlBreadcrumbs) in failure-summary.json but never used it during RCA | Data generation ≠ data consumption — agent instructions never directed agents to read artifact paths | Instruction architecture must explicitly direct agents to consume every data field produced. When adding a new field to diagnostic output, ALSO add a corresponding agent instruction step referencing it | Copilot | 2026-02-24 |
| LRN-007 | DATA | `inputValue()` returns "4.00%" not "0.04" for percentage spinbuttons | Display format ≠ input format — Angular formats after blur | Verify `inputValue()` return via MCP `browser_evaluate` before writing assertions. Build comparison logic AFTER confirming display vs raw format | Generator | 2026-02-24 |
| LRN-008 | SELECTOR | Triple-click fails on Angular spin re-render — input value not cleared | Angular re-renders input on focus event, invalidating the triple-click selection | Use `Ctrl+A → type replacement` instead of triple-click select-all for Angular spinbutton inputs | Generator | 2026-02-24 |
| LRN-009 | LOGIC | `test.describe.serial` first-test failure cascades ALL remaining to skip — zero diagnostic data | Serial describe = single point of failure; if TC-001 fails, entire suite is blind | Ensure TC-001 (navigation) is rock-solid with extra timeout + networkidle wait; if it fails, no data for any other test | Generator | 2026-02-24 |
| LRN-010 | DATA | Valid-case boundary test in `describe.serial` fails with unexpected display value (e.g. "got value=4.00") | Invalid test before it returned `passed: false` without restoring DB value — next test reads dirty state | Fix the invalid case to ALWAYS restore before returning; do not adjust valid case assertion. Restore path must run on both pass and fail branches | Healer | 2026-02-25 |
| LRN-011 | LOGIC | Agent diagnosed wrong failing TC — spent effort on test that was already removed | Accepted user's description of failing TC label without running spec first to see actual output | ALWAYS run spec first, read exact failing TC name from terminal output. User description ≠ test title. `"0.01"` and `"-0.01"` are different tests | Healer | 2026-02-25 |
| LRN-012 | LOGIC | TC-037 (error recovery): Angular disables Save when spinbutton has an inline max-violation error — invalid value never reaches DB | Angular form marks control invalid on blur for boundary violations (both min and max) AND disables the Save button. The test plan claim "invalid values persist to DB" applies only to server-side validators, not Angular client-side ones | Do NOT attempt to save invalid spinbutton values to DB via setSpinValue+clickSave — Save will be no-op. For boundary violation tests, use client-side inline error detection only (blur + hasValidationError). Mark tests requiring DB persistence of invalid spinbutton values as Cat-B FIXME. | Generator | 2026-02-25 |
| LRN-013 | FORMAT | `fillText()` saved old value to DB — test expected new value, got original | `page.fill()` / `el.fill()` does NOT fire Angular's `blur` or `change` events. Angular's form model never commits the new value, so Save sends the prior value to the API. | Always call `await el.press('Tab')` after `el.fill()` on Angular textboxes to force the form model to commit. Verified fix for `txtOracleProduct` and applies to all Angular-bound text inputs. | Generator | 2026-02-25 |
| LRN-014 | INFRASTRUCTURE | `Stop-Process -Name node` kills MCP browser during test cleanup | MCP server (@playwright/mcp) runs on Node — blanket node kill destroys it along with auth session and inspection state | Use targeted process filtering: `Get-CimInstance Win32_Process -Filter "Name='node.exe'" \| Where { CommandLine -match 'playwright.*test' }`. Never blanket-kill node. See GEN-037, ALL-021 | Copilot | 2026-02-25 |
| LRN-015 | SELECTOR | All planner-provided currency selectors failed at runtime (`input[type="checkbox"]`, `cell:text-is()`, `[role="columnheader"]`, `tabpanel:has(...)`) | App uses Radix UI: checkboxes are `<button role="checkbox">` not `<input type="checkbox">`. `cell` is not valid CSS (use `td`). `<th>` has no explicit `role="columnheader"`. `<tabpanel>` is not an HTML element. | ALWAYS run `browser_snapshot` pre-flight for EVERY selector before first test run (Phase 3). Planner "live verified" selectors may target wrong element type if Radix/ShadCN UI library is used. Don't trust — verify. | Generator | 2026-02-25 |
| LRN-016 | LOGIC | Unchecking the last Selected currency in Currency tab auto-unchecks its IsDefault — restore must re-check BOTH | Radix UI checkbox dependency: `Selected=false` cascades to `IsDefault=false`. If test only restores Selected without IsDefault, DB saves corrupted baseline for next serial test | In `test.describe.serial`, always restore BOTH the target field AND its dependent fields. For currency: `checkCheckbox('chkUSDSelected')` + `checkCheckbox('chkUSDIsDefault')` + `clickSave()` | Generator | 2026-02-25 |
| LRN-017 | SELECTOR | `<next-location-settings>` shadow DOM wraps all location settings content | App uses Angular custom element with shadow root — `document.querySelector()` can't reach children, but Playwright's CSS engine auto-pierces | No special `>>` combinator needed. But `browser_evaluate('document.querySelector(...)')` in MCP will NOT find shadow children — use `browser_snapshot` + accessibility tree instead, or `page.locator()` which auto-pierces | Generator | 2026-02-25 |
| LRN-018 | LOGIC | TC-013 planner expected error dialog on zero-currency save, but app disables Save instead | Angular/Radix form validation disables Save when business rule fails (0 currencies) rather than showing post-click error. Same pattern as LRN-012 (spinbutton max violation disables Save) | When TC says "click Save → error", verify via browser_snapshot that Save is actually enabled first. If Save is disabled, the business rule fires on change, not on submit. Adapt test to assert disabled state, update TC Steps | Generator | 2026-02-25 |
| LRN-019 | NAVIGATION | MCP `page.goto(sameUrl)` may reuse Angular component without server refetch — snapshot shows stale optimistic form values | Angular router's route reuse strategy can keep component alive on same-URL navigation; the accessibility tree reflects the in-memory form state, not a fresh server response | To verify true server-persisted state: navigate AWAY to a different route first (e.g. `#/setup/locationlist`), THEN navigate back. `reloadAndNavigateToLocalInfo()` correctly does this. Direct same-URL goto in MCP is unreliable for persistence verification | Generator | 2026-02-27 |
| LRN-020 | DATA | Training server for office 1604 silently rejects ALL persistent field changes (LDW%, Billing Type, Oracle Product, Oracle Department, etc.) | The training environment appears to have a server-side read-only constraint on office 1604 fields — confirmed via MCP: save dialog confirmed → reload → server returns original/grandfathered values without any error signal | Mark all save+reload persistence tests for office 1604 as `test.skip(true, 'Cat-B: server silently rejects...')`. In BoundaryCase data, use `pending: 'Cat-B: ...'` and check `bc.pending` in the test loop. Confirmed: LDW/BillingType/OracleProduct/OracleDept all revert | Generator | 2026-02-27 |
| LRN-021 | CONFIG | `viewport: null` in Playwright config causes headless runs to use narrow default viewport — Navigator Cloud's responsive sidebar collapses, Setup button absent from DOM, auth fixture times out at 60s | `viewport: null` means "use browser default" in headless mode (not "maximize"). Browser default is ~800x600 or similar, too narrow for the app's min-width sidebar threshold | Set `viewport: { width: 1920, height: 1080 }` in both global `use` and the `chromium` project block. `null` only works reliably in headed mode with `--start-maximized`. Never use `null` for responsive apps running headless | Generator | 2026-02-27 |
| LRN-022 | SCOPE | User invoked `audit` but audit agent re-audited already-covered work instead of starting from the last logged audit entry | No defined temporal anchor for audit scope — agent defaulted to re-scanning all history | When user says `audit` (any mode), FIRST read `agent-activity-log.md`, identify the last `audit` action entry, and scope ALL checks to work done AFTER that timestamp. Do not re-audit already-covered periods. The pattern: last audit entry timestamp → everything after that timestamp = unaudited scope. Log this scope boundary at start of report | Audit | 2026-02-27 |